    "description": "British Mandate era; valley agriculture",
    "notes": "Historic 1,050 mm line (this). The modern namesake (2016) is a separate standard-gauge build — see historic_vs_modern.  [description] 'British Mandate era' is imprecise: the line OPENED IN 1905 UNDER OTTOMAN RULE as part of the Hejaz Haifa-Deraa branch; it merely OPERATED during the later British Mandate.  [route] ORDER CORRECTED: the project list had Tzemah before Gesher/Naharayim, but by km-post (Beit She’an 59.3 km; Tzemah 86.9 km; al-Hamma 95.3 km) the order east of Beit She’an is Gesher -> Naharayim -> Samakh/Tzemah -> al-Hamma. Added the missing Kfar Yehoshua and Beit She’an. Naharayim (Rutenberg hydro site, 1930s) is a later halt near the Jordan confluence.  [historic_vs_modern] CRITICAL DISTINCTION — two different railways share this name: (1) the HISTORIC Jezreel Valley line (this one) = 1905, 1,050 mm NARROW gauge, Haifa->Afula->Beit She’an->Gesher->Naharayim->Samakh->al-Hamma (->Deraa), closed 1948 (Haifa-Afula to 1949); and (2) the MODERN 'New Jezreel Valley railway' (Israel Railways, opened 16 Oct 2016) = STANDARD gauge 1,435 mm, Haifa->Beit She’an ONLY (~60 km) on a partly-new alignment. The modern line does NOT continue east to Gesher, Naharayim, Tzemah or al-Hamma — so the four eastern stops in this list exist ONLY on the historic line.  [relationship] This route OVERLAPS the kit’s 'Haifa-Deraa Line': the Jezreel Valley line is the western/central portion of that same Hejaz branch (Haifa-Deraa additionally climbs the Yarmuk gorge to Deraa). Keep the relationship explicit in the DB to avoid double-counting shared stations.",
    "history": "Opened 1905 at 1,050 mm as the western/central part of the Hejaz Haifa-Deraa branch, running from the Mediterranean at Haifa up the Jezreel and Harod valleys to the Jordan valley (Beit She'an, Gesher, Naharayim, Samakh/Tzemah) and al-Hamma on the Yarmuk. Known for serving the valley's agriculture; al-Hamma sits at today's Israel/Jordan/Syria tri-border.",
    "verification_status": "unverified",
    "source_ids": [
      "levantrain_system",
      "shemer_jezreel",
      "wp_israel_rw",
      "wp_jezreel"
    ]
  },
